{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And the waters prevailed one hundred and fifty days.</b> From the day the rain began they prevailed until the completion of one hundred and fifty days. The rain began on the seventeenth of the second month and was completed on the seventeenth of the seventh month, the one hundred and fifty days being five full months, and then the ark came to rest, since there was no further prevailing force to drive it. For indeed from the day the rain began, the prevailing force began from below, as it says: <b>all the fountains of the great deep burst forth</b>. However, the ark did not begin to move upon the face of the waters until the waters were so high that the ark was lifted above the earth, and when the days of rain were completed, the prevailing force from below alone continued until the one hundred and fifty days were full, and then, when the prevailing force that drove the ark ceased, the ark came to rest."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:34.490840651Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}